<section class="portal-page" data-portal-panel="about">
<div class="portal-page-title"><span class="portal-kicker">Help &amp; guide</span><h1>How to use AquaDissect</h1><p>Find guidance for account access, class activities, and recorded progress.</p></div>
<div id="tutorialGuides"></div><div class="workspace-panel"><h2>Quick reference</h2><label for="helpSearch">Search help topics</label><input id="helpSearch" type="search" placeholder="Try accounts, offline, or results"><p id="helpEmpty" hidden>No matching help topics.</p>
<details class="help-topic"><summary>Activate a student account</summary><p>Use the institutional email and one-time activation code supplied by your administrator. Set your own password. Research consent remains separate from account activation.</p></details><details class="help-topic"><summary>Request instructor access</summary><p>Open Instructor registration from the login page. An administrator must approve your account and assign your MB 304L sections before you can manage class activities.</p></details><details class="help-topic"><summary>Start a lesson</summary><p>Open Safety &amp; Tools and complete your required module first. Then open an assigned species lesson from your class section. Explore labels, follow the guided sequence, and complete the formative checks.</p></details><details class="help-topic"><summary>Manage people and sections</summary><p>Administrators provision accounts, assign instructors, and preview roster imports in People &amp; sections. Table search, column sorting, and pagination help find records. Expand a row to see its actions.</p></details><details class="help-topic"><summary>Use the class calendar</summary><p>View schedules in month, week, day, or list format. All displayed times use Philippine time. Staff may add or cancel events in authorized sections. Cancelled events remain visible for reference.</p></details><details class="help-topic"><summary>Read notifications</summary><p>The bell shows unread updates. Open Notifications to review new assignments, class events, account approvals, and content decisions. Mark individual updates or the whole inbox as read.</p></details><details class="help-topic"><summary>Understand learning reports</summary><p>Reports show recorded formative attempts and safety progress. Filter by section, date, and activity, then download CSV. Unattributed historical records are kept separate from class summaries. These operational records do not establish learning effectiveness.</p></details><details class="help-topic"><summary>Study offline and synchronize</summary><p>While signed in, download assigned lessons from Offline access. Downloaded materials and your learning context stay on this device. Queued work synchronizes only with the same account after reconnection. Sign out when sharing a device; reconnect and sign in again to restore your learning context.</p></details><details class="help-topic"><summary>Review and publish content</summary><p>Instructors submit prepared content for faculty review. Publication still requires the existing approval rules. Administrators publish approved versions; learners receive only authorized published lessons.</p></details><details class="help-topic"><summary>Get account support</summary><p>Contact your administrator for activation, enrollment, approval, or password assistance. Never share your password with another learner.</p></details></div></section>
